# elvis (vi) translation units: netbsd-0-9's elvis 1.x from
# vendor/netbsd-0-9/usr.bin/elvis (ruled the porting source for this tool),
# with five TUs replaced by FGX copies in this directory.  main.c is the entry
# (manifest "main"); these are the rest.
#
# system.c is the machine-layer seam.  modify.c is verbatim except that add()'s
# two BLK locals are static -- a 4 KB frame stack_measure charges to vi twice
# (fn-ptr and signal one-hop allowances); its header says why that is safe and
# why not CRUNCH.  unix.c is the vendored BSD backend: it selects on fd 0
# (apple/fgx#151).
